\newlabel{sec:c06-redblack}{{8.4}{509}{Red-Black Trees (Why \code {std::set} Is Fast)}{section.8.4}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {8.4.1}Intuition}{510}{subsection.8.4.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.4.1}{\ignorespaces Red-black insertion repair, given a red parent (which already breaks the no-adjacent-red rule with the freshly-inserted red node). \textbf  {(a)} If the \emph  {uncle is red}, no rotation: recolour parent and uncle black, grandparent red, and treat the grandparent as the new ``red node to check'' -- the fix hops one level up. \textbf  {(b)} If the uncle is \emph  {black} and the red nodes form a straight \emph  {line}, rotate about the grandparent and swap two colours. \textbf  {(c)} If they form a \emph  {bend}, do the LR/RL double rotation first to make a line, then case (b). Case (a) is red-black's signature -- it fixes by \emph  {flipping bits}, which AVL never gets to do.}}{511}{figure.caption.88}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c06-rbfix}{{8.4.1}{511}{Red-black insertion repair, given a red parent (which already breaks the no-adjacent-red rule with the freshly-inserted red node). \textbf {(a)} If the \emph {uncle is red}, no rotation: recolour parent and uncle black, grandparent red, and treat the grandparent as the new ``red node to check'' -- the fix hops one level up. \textbf {(b)} If the uncle is \emph {black} and the red nodes form a straight \emph {line}, rotate about the grandparent and swap two colours. \textbf {(c)} If they form a \emph {bend}, do the LR/RL double rotation first to make a line, then case (b). Case (a) is red-black's signature -- it fixes by \emph {flipping bits}, which AVL never gets to do}{figure.caption.88}{}}
